@startuml
title UC-14 - Enforce Application Rule (planned FST-028)
autonumber
participant "DetectDistractionUseCase" as Detect
participant "BlockDistractionUseCase" as Block
participant "Session / policy reader" as Current
participant "ApplicationBlockerPort" as Port
participant "OS adapter" as OS
participant "Transactional outbox" as Outbox
participant "Outbox dispatcher" as Dispatch
participant "Log projection / WebSocket" as Consumers

Detect -> Block : enforce(detectionId, decision, transient instance)
Block -> Current : recheck RUNNING + WORK, rule enabled, target match
Current --> Block : eligible / stale
alt eligible
  Block -> Port : block observed application instance
  Port -> OS : revalidate instance; apply supported operation
  note right of OS
    Platform operation and permissions require FST-028 approval.
    Do not act on a different process after PID reuse.
  end note
  OS --> Port : confirmed / failed / already exited
  Port --> Block : explicit outcome
  alt confirmed enforcement
    Block -> Outbox : append DistractionBlocked(detectionId)
  else failed / permission denied / unavailable
    Block -> Outbox : append DistractionBlockFailed(detectionId, reason)
  else already exited
    note right of Block : No remaining target to enforce; safe no-op.
  end
  Block -> Outbox : commit outcome transaction, if any
  Dispatch -> Outbox : read committed outcome events
  Outbox --> Dispatch : outcome
  Dispatch -> Consumers : project / notify idempotently
else stale decision
  note right of Block : Cancel operation; do not claim blocking success.
end
note over Port, Outbox
  OS side effect and event commit are not atomic.
  Recording failures require diagnostics and cleanup tracking.
  Event delivery does not replay the OS operation.
end note
@enduml
